  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/dburriss/flexi-json",
  "published": "2026-11-17T18:02:05.44Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "`JsonParsed`, `JsonValue.ParseWithMetadata` and `JsonValue.TryParseWithMetadata`: return the root, the spans and the original text of every number (`NumberText`, keyed by JSON Pointer), so `1.10`, `1E+2` and integers beyond int64 can be recovered exactly. Existing signatures and behaviour are unchanged.\nTargets `netstandard2.0` and `net10.0` instead of `netstandard2.0` and `net8.0`, since .NET 8 went out of support on 2026-11-10. Projects on .NET 8 and 9 use the `netstandard2.0` build.",
